# The index holds LF, as git normalizes text, and every checkout gets CRLF, which is what
# .editorconfig asks for, whatever core.autocrlf says on the machine. Before this file existed the
# working tree was CRLF only on clones with autocrlf on, and scripts/version-manager.ps1's CRLF
# write produced a whole-file diff on the others. SourceHygieneTests pins this line.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Belt and braces: text=auto detects these, but a misdetected icon or image would be corrupted on checkout.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.pfx binary
